==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|astrologer}}, {{m|enm|astrologier}}, {{m|enm|astrologere}}, formed from {{der|en|enm|astrologie}} or {{der|en|la|astrologus}} + {{der|en|enm|-ere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|astrology|-er|id2=occupation}}. Ousted imported {{noncog|enm|astrologien|t=astrologer}}, borrowed from {{noncog|fro|astrologien}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|tungolwītga|lit=star prophet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈstrɒl.ə.d͡ʒə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Arlo Barnes-astrologer.wav|}}

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun|plural|astrologers|feminine|astrologess}}

# One who studies or practices [[astrology]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|astrologist}}

